     "content": "**Yes, you should accept this offer.** \n\nGetting a **$200,000 cash sign-on bonus** alongside a $1.08M equity grant at Google L6 is an exceptional outcome. It completely eliminates the financial friction of walking away from your unvested Meta RSUs and catapults your near-term earnings well above market.\n\n---\n\n### The Numbers: How It Breaks Down\n\nWith Google's standard front-loaded vesting schedule (**33% / 33% / 22% / 12%**), your compensation profile looks like this:\n\n| Year | Base | Target Bonus (20%) | Initial RSUs | Sign-On Bonus | **Total Comp (excl. Refreshes)** | vs. Meta Run Rate (~$526k) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Year 1** | $240,000 | $48,000 | $356,400 (33%) | $200,000 | **~$844,400** | **+$318,400** *(+$368k vs next 12mo)* |\n| **Year 2** | $240,000 | $48,000 | $356,400 (33%) | $0 | **~$644,400** | **+$118,400** |\n| **Year 3** | $240,000 | $48,000 | $237,600 (22%) | $0 | **~$525,600** *(+ refreshers)* | Break-even (before refreshers) |\n| **Year 4** | $240,000 | $48,000 | $129,600 (12%) | $0 | **~$417,600** *(+ refreshers)* | Refresher dependent |\n\n* **4-Year Guaranteed Total:** **~$2.43M** (an average of **~$608,000/year** before any equity appreciation or annual refreshers).\n* **The First 2 Years:** You will make nearly **$1.5M in cash and vested equity over your first 24 months**.\n\n---\n\n### Why This Is a Clear \"Take It\"\n\n1. **They fully insured your unvested equity with guaranteed cash:** Instead of promising higher hypothetical future equity, they handed you **$200,000 in liquid cash** to offset what you're leaving behind at Meta.\n2. **Top-of-market L6 package:** $200k sign-on bonuses at L6 are rare and reserved for competitive buyouts against Tier-1 peers (Meta, Apple, Netflix). There is virtually no remaining headroom at this level without an L7 down-level/up-level discussion.\n3. **Massive Year 1 upside:** At ~$844k in Year 1, you are earning executive-level compensation while maintaining standard Senior PM (IC6/L6) scope.\n\n---\n\n### 3 Quick Things to Check Before You Sign\n\n1. **Sign-on payment & clawback terms:** Clarify if the $200,000 is paid as a lump sum in your first 30 days or split across Year 1 and Year 2 (e.g., $100k Y1 / $100k Y2), and check the standard 12-to-24 month pro-rated clawback clause.\n2. **Team & scope alignment:** Make sure you're excited about your specific product area, manager, and org charter. Google PM culture is much more consensus-driven and matrixed than Meta's bottom-up, ship-fast culture.\n3. **Start date timing:** Ensure your start date allows you to capture any imminent Meta bonus or vesting events right before you give notice.",
